  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ID: Center for Victims of Torture- Helping Survivors Heal</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(USAID Bureau for Inclusive Growth, Partnerships, and Innovation (IPI)):  The Helping Suvivors Heal activity enhances the effectiveness of local service providers for survivors of torture and build mental health and psychosocial support (MHPSS) workforce capacity to expand access to quality, evidence-based services adapted to local contexts, with explicit attention to gender and social inclusion. The activity is a collaborative partnerships between the Center for Victims of Torture and 12 local providers of MHPSS services to survivors of torture in the Global South.  In FY 2024,a particular focus will be on the 12 partners to provide organizational diversity (e.g., size, client population, geography) and enrich cross partner learning and project impact, but allow for deep and holistic capacity support.   The program contributes to the Agency&apos;s development and foreign policy objectives by - among other things - improving well-being and resilience, and promoting peace and stability. This IM implements the Victims of Torture directive/earmark.</narrative>
  </description>
